# PeekStox: full build prompt (instructions + code)

Copy everything below this line into your AI coding tool.

---

ROLE
You are a senior front-end engineer and UI designer working on "PeekStox", a stock-market research
web app: React + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 (`@import "tailwindcss"`), lucide-react, Vite.
Reference mockups are attached (laptop, tablet, phone; dark and light). Match them closely.
If this text and an image disagree, the image wins for look; this text wins for behaviour,
accessibility and data rules.

HOW TO USE THIS PROMPT
1. The sections under "FILES" contain the complete reference implementation. Create or overwrite
   each file at exactly the path shown. Edit only those files. Do not rewrite unrelated files.
2. Keep existing props, data types and API routes. The other screens (Explorer, Compare, Algo Lab,
   AI, Watchlist, Overview, News, Settings, modals) and `src/components/PeekStoxLogo.tsx` already
   exist: leave them unchanged. Delete `src/styles/responsive.css` if it exists; `index.css` now
   contains everything and App.tsx no longer imports it.
3. The code uses English strings. If the project has a translation function, wrap the labels with
   it and keep an English fallback. Never render a raw key such as "dashboard" or "algo".
4. `GlobalIndex.name` and the `NewsItem` fields (title, source, time, image, url) are read
   defensively in DashboardView. If the project's types differ, adapt minimally and say so.
5. After applying the files, run the acceptance checks in section 6 and report what you could
   not verify.

PRODUCT FEEL
Premium, calm, data-dense but never cluttered. "Liquid glass": frosted translucent surfaces over
soft coloured light. Dark mode = glowing green and violet on near-black. Light mode = warm cream
paper with sage green and tan. Both themes must feel like one product.

=====================================================================
1. NAVIGATION ITEMS (real screens)
=====================================================================
Primary: Markets (dashboard), Explorer, Watchlist, Financial News, PeekStox AI (assistant).
Tools: Compare, Quantitative Lab (algo), Global Overview (overview).
Account: Market Alerts (opens the alerts modal, shows unread count), Settings, About Us, profile
card (avatar, name, role). Route ids: dashboard, explorer, compare, algo, assistant, watchlist,
overview, news, settings, about.

=====================================================================
2. HOW THE LAYOUT ADAPTS (by available width, never by device name)
=====================================================================
Window classes (detect with matchMedia change events, not resize spam):
  compact  <600px        phones, foldable cover screen
  medium   600-1023px    tablet portrait, unfolded foldable, small windows
  expanded >=1024px      laptops, desktops, tablet landscape
  extra    >=1280px      Markets switches to two independent columns
Rules that always hold:
- Exactly ONE primary navigation at a time: floating dock (compact, medium) OR left sidebar
  (expanded, or foldable spanning two screens). Never both. CSS also hides the dock at >=1024px
  as a safeguard.
- Respect safe-area insets (top, bottom, left, right). The viewport meta tag needs
  `viewport-fit=cover`.
- Page gutter 16 / 24 / 32px (compact / medium / expanded). Card radius 20px, inner tiles 12px,
  pills fully round. Content max width 1200px, centred.
- Type: page title 20/24/28px bold; hero number 30/36/48px bold with tabular numerals; card label
  12px uppercase letter-spaced; body 14px; nothing below 12px.
- NEVER hide a layout bug with overflow-x:hidden. At 360-430px nothing may scroll sideways; fix
  the cause (min-w-0 on flex/grid children, fixed widths, wide rows).
- Header is sticky, translucent glass, 56-64px tall. Sidebar is sticky, full height.

---------------------------------------------------------------------
2A. PHONE (360-599px, portrait): single column, compact cards
---------------------------------------------------------------------
Header: brand mark (hidden under 380px) + page title left; 44px icon buttons for Search and
Alerts; a small "Live" chip (dot + word, no refresh icon); avatar button. No full search field, no
price strip, no theme button (theme lives in Settings).

FLOATING LIQUID-GLASS DOCK (not a docked full-width bar):
- Fixed, centred, floating above the bottom edge: bottom = safe-area-inset-bottom + 12px;
  width = min(100vw - 24px, 416px); radius 28px; padding 6px.
- Glass: dark = white gradient overlay + rgb(14 16 20 / .68), blur(26px) saturate(190%), 1px
  border rgb(255 255 255 / .16), bright inset top rim, soft sheen, deep shadow. Light = ivory
  gradient rgb(255 252 244 / .94) to rgb(244 236 221 / .76), white border, warm shadow. It must
  be opaque enough that page text never shows through or collides with the labels.
- Five items, icon above a 12px label, each at least 52px tall: Markets, Explorer, Watchlist,
  AI, More. Active item = tinted pill with a soft glow (dark: green tint; light: tan tint
  rgb(120 92 40 / .13)), aria-current="page". Items are real links (#/view).
- "More" opens a bottom sheet (role=dialog, aria-modal, Esc closes, Tab trapped, focus returns to
  More) listing Compare, Quantitative Lab, Global Overview, Financial News, Settings, About Us,
  Market Alerts (with unread count). Unread badge on More.
- Page content gets bottom padding = dock height + offset + safe area, so nothing hides behind it.

COMPACT MARKETS SCREEN (goal: about 1.5 screens tall, like the phone mockup). Order:
  1. Hero card (padding 12px): label, index name, glowing change pill, 30px level number, chart
     only ~80px tall with glowing end dot. Benchmark chips are hidden here (they live in the
     enlarged view).
  2. Two cards side by side: Market Sentiment (small gauge, "17 of 48 up") | AI Analyst (36px orb
     + 4 lines of 12px text). No "Ask AI" link here.
  3. Technical Indicators: left a 2x2 grid of tiny tiles (short labels RSI, MACD, MA, BB under
     420px; mini chart 24px; value; state word is screen-reader-only), right a "Trend" tile with a
     dotted projection, a change pill and the words "Not advice".
  4. Watchlist: exactly 3 cards in one row (ticker, price, change stacked; 20px sparkline).
  5. Live Activity: ONE single-line glass pill, truncated, no extra buttons.
  6. News: 3 compact rows (40px thumbnail, 2-line headline, source and time).
TAP TO ENLARGE (phones only): every small card (hero, sentiment, AI, each indicator tile, trend
tile, watchlist stock, news row) opens an enlarged view, like an image preview:
- Implement with a stretched invisible button over the card (aria-label "Expand <name>",
  aria-haspopup="dialog") plus a small expand icon in the corner; interactive children stay
  clickable above it.
- Enlarged view = centred glass panel (width 100% - 24px, max 640px, height fit-content, scroll
  inside if tall), blurred dimmed backdrop, title, a 44px close X top-right, scale-in animation
  (180ms, disabled for reduced motion). Esc, backdrop tap and X all close it. Render through a
  portal to <body> so the dock can never sit on top of it. Lock body scroll while open, trap
  focus, restore focus to the opener on close.
- Contents: Hero = big level, pill, 208px chart, day high/low, status, updated time, and the
  benchmark chips. Sentiment = full gauge, the rule (above 60% Bullish, below 40% Bearish), top 3
  gainers and top 3 decliners. AI = larger orb, full summary built from numbers (breadth, biggest
  mover, leading and lagging sector), "Ask PeekStox AI" button. Indicator = big value, state,
  larger chart, plain-language explanation, and how many data points are needed if not ready.
  Trend = bigger chart with dotted projection and the not-a-forecast note. Stock = price, change,
  chart, day/52-week high and low, volume, exchange, "Open in Explorer". News = image, headline,
  source/time, "Read article" if a URL exists.
- On tablet and laptop, cards do NOT pop open (watchlist items navigate to Explorer, news items
